      "comment": "PHOENIX AMELIA (4) hit the ground running to win over the 457m at this track two runs back then settled forward again when finishing second at this track last start. Safe beginner but has a tricky box to overcome. Key chance in this line up. CHRISTMAS DAY (1) was strong over this course and distance last time despite filling the minors, finishing 0.8 lengths behind Brunswick Rocket in 25.63 and recording a new PB here. Rates a leading chance if runs up to latest. LUCORA (2) carved over from wide out and boxed on strongly to finish 1.75 lengths away in third (25.70) behind Brunswick Rocket at this track. Hard to beat again. NON STOP WHISKEY (3) has claims fresh from a recent placing in good time.",
